Cassie, you got a mercury color.
凯西，你拿到的是水银色的。

1314
00:51:47.550 --> 00:51:48.210
It's called mercury.
这颜色叫水银色。

1315
00:51:48.450 --> 00:51:49.010
Ooh, mercury.
噢，水银色。

1316
00:51:49.310 --> 00:51:49.650
Tim.
蒂姆。

1317
00:51:50.070 --> 00:51:50.250
Okay.
好的。

1318
00:51:50.250 --> 00:51:51.910
You got...
你拿到的是……

1319
00:51:51.910 --> 00:51:53.410
Oh, silver.
噢，银色的。

1320
00:51:53.750 --> 00:51:54.390
Thank you.
谢谢。

1321
00:51:54.690 --> 00:51:56.150
And I got navy.
我的是海军蓝的。

1322
00:51:56.570 --> 00:51:57.950
I understand now.
我现在明白了。

1323
00:51:58.010 --> 00:52:00.690
It's just a short-sleeve puffer jacket.
它就是一件短袖羽绒服。

1324
00:52:00.870 --> 00:52:04.050
It's a puffer jacket that looks like a t-shirt when you put it on.
这是一款穿上后看起来像T恤的羽绒服。

1325
00:52:04.050 --> 00:52:10.070
Instead of being a long-sleeve jacket or a vest, it is a short-sleeve puffer jacket.
它不是长袖夹克也不是马甲，而是短袖羽绒服。

1326
00:52:10.310 --> 00:52:10.690
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1327
00:52:11.130 --> 00:52:11.450
All right.
好吧。

1328
00:52:11.550 --> 00:52:11.930
Hold on.
等一下。

1329
00:52:11.930 --> 00:52:12.570
I'll put mine on.
我把我的穿上。

1330
00:52:12.590 --> 00:52:13.050
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1331
00:52:13.050 --> 00:52:13.890
I'll get you the right size.
我去给你们拿合适的尺码。

1332
00:52:13.890 --> 00:52:14.270
There's pockets.
还有口袋。

1333
00:52:14.730 --> 00:52:15.430
There's pockets.
还有口袋。

1334
00:52:15.830 --> 00:52:16.450
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1335
00:52:16.570 --> 00:52:17.570
Sam, you look amazing.
萨姆，你看起来棒极了。

1336
00:52:18.230 --> 00:52:20.090
Oh, and the pockets are, like, fleece.
噢，而且口袋里好像是抓绒的。

1337
00:52:20.390 --> 00:52:21.030
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1338
00:52:21.350 --> 00:52:22.010
Ooh, comfy.
噢，真舒服。

1339
00:52:22.370 --> 00:52:23.450
Did I get the right sizes?
我尺码买对了吗？

1340
00:52:23.650 --> 00:52:24.250
You sure did.
你绝对买对了。

1341
00:52:24.410 --> 00:52:25.170
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1342
00:52:25.170 --> 00:52:26.370
You guys look amazing.
你们看起来都太棒了。

1343
00:52:27.810 --> 00:52:28.470
All right.
好了。

1344
00:52:28.670 --> 00:52:29.050
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1345
00:52:29.050 --> 00:52:30.830
Happy holidays, everybody.
祝大家节日快乐。

1346
00:52:31.310 --> 00:52:32.670
Thank you, Shannikin.
谢谢你，香妮金。

1347
00:52:33.070 --> 00:52:33.630
You're welcome.
不客气。

1348
00:52:36.270 --> 00:52:37.570
That was amazing.
这太棒了。

1349
00:52:37.830 --> 00:52:39.450
Angela, you really brought it today.
安吉拉，你今天真是太给力了。

1350
00:52:39.550 --> 00:52:42.770
How'd you get all this stuff in here without me seeing it?
你是怎么在我不注意的情况下把这些东西都弄进来的？

1351
00:52:42.810 --> 00:52:43.890
I had to make two trips.
我得跑两趟才行。

1352
00:52:43.890 --> 00:52:46.050
How many bags of stuff did you bring in?
你带了多少袋东西进来？

1353
00:52:46.230 --> 00:52:47.450
I had to make two trips.
我得跑两趟才行。

1354
00:52:47.710 --> 00:52:50.290
I made one trip and hid stuff in our desk area.
我跑了一趟，把东西藏在我们的办公桌区了。

1355
00:52:50.510 --> 00:52:50.830
Okay.
好吧。

1356
00:52:51.130 --> 00:52:51.850
For a week.
持续了一周。

1357
00:52:52.610 --> 00:52:54.530
And then I brought everything else today.
然后我今天把剩下的都带来了。

1358
00:52:55.070 --> 00:52:57.030
There are some other people exchanging gifts.
还有其他人在交换礼物。

1359
00:52:57.170 --> 00:52:58.090
They are Jim and Pam.
他们是吉姆和帕姆。

1360
00:52:58.090 --> 00:52:59.470
It's finally time.
终于到了这一刻。

1361
00:52:59.750 --> 00:53:00.950
They're in the break room.
他们在休息室里。

1362
00:53:01.350 --> 00:53:04.210
Yes, I am calling this Christmas in the break room.
没错，我把这称为休息室里的圣诞节。

1363
00:53:04.410 --> 00:53:07.210
You know, we had a fan question from Bill S.
你知道，我们收到了一位来自新罕布什尔州梅里马克市的粉丝比尔·S的提问，

1364
00:53:07.390 --> 00:53:11.510
in Merrimack, New Hampshire, and many others who wrote in to say,
还有许多其他人也写信来说，

1365
00:53:11.690 --> 00:53:14.890
Pam and Jim are married and have a child at home.
帕姆和吉姆已经结婚了，家里还有个孩子。

1366
00:53:15.050 --> 00:53:19.550
They presumably give each other gifts at home on Christmas Day like families do.
他们理应像其他家庭一样，在圣诞节当天在家里互赠礼物。

1367
00:53:19.810 --> 00:53:24.390
So why do they give one another their most special presents at the office?
那为什么他们要在办公室里给对方送最特别的礼物呢？

1368
00:53:24.430 --> 00:53:26.430
This has never made sense to me.
这对我来说一直都说不通。

1369
00:53:26.430 --> 00:53:28.470
It's a valid question.
这确实是个好问题。

1370
00:53:28.790 --> 00:53:34.770
And if I am sort of living in the world of the show, Jim and Pam met at Dunder Mifflin.
如果我把自己代入剧中的世界，吉姆和帕姆是在邓德·米夫林相识的。

1371
00:53:34.970 --> 00:53:39.630
The first gift exchange they ever had that really meant something to the two of them for their
他们第一次真正对彼此有意义的礼物交换，

1372
00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:41.350
relationship happened there.
就是在那段关系中发生的。

1373
00:53:41.350 --> 00:53:51.770
I could see it being sort of a very sweet couple tradition that they sneak away somewhere in the office and they give each other a gift because of that very first Christmas.
我觉得这可能是一种非常甜蜜的夫妻传统，因为那个最初的圣诞节，他们会偷偷溜到办公室的某个地方给对方送礼物。

1374
00:53:52.250 --> 00:53:57.590
Angela, that is exactly what John and I decided on set during this episode.
安吉拉，那正是约翰和我在这集拍摄现场商量好的。

1375
00:53:57.690 --> 00:53:58.110
Yay!
耶！

1376
00:53:58.110 --> 00:53:59.670
We asked the same question.
我们也问过同样的问题。

1377
00:53:59.870 --> 00:54:02.830
We said, why would they give each other their big Christmas gift at work?
我们说，为什么他们要在工作时给对方送重要的圣诞礼物呢？

1378
00:54:02.970 --> 00:54:03.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1379
00:54:03.450 --> 00:54:04.550
It's a little odd.
这确实有点奇怪。

1380
00:54:04.650 --> 00:54:06.190
And we talked about it as a group.
我们大家讨论过这个问题。

1381
00:54:06.190 --> 00:54:07.830
And that is exactly what we said.
而那正是我们得出的结论。

1382
00:54:08.270 --> 00:54:12.590
And the other thing we said was that it's supposed to be a homemade gift.
我们还说，这礼物应该是手工制作的。

1383
00:54:12.590 --> 00:54:20.350
So each year, in the tradition of the teapot and all of that, that they're going to exchange a little homemade item at the office.
所以每年，秉承着茶壶以及诸如此类的传统，他们要在办公室交换一件小小的手工制品。

1384
00:54:20.870 --> 00:54:27.490
Remember, there was that whole deleted runner, that one Christmas episode, where Pam and Jim are making gifts for one another.
还记得吗，在某一集圣诞特辑里，有一段被删减的剧情，讲的是帕姆和吉姆为彼此制作礼物。

1385
00:54:27.690 --> 00:54:29.470
From things that they found in the office?
用在办公室里找到的东西？

1386
00:54:29.550 --> 00:54:29.810
Yes.
是的。

1387
00:54:29.810 --> 00:54:31.210
So this is the tradition.
所以这就是他们的传统。

1388
00:54:31.510 --> 00:54:32.710
That makes total sense.
这完全说得通。

1389
00:54:32.870 --> 00:54:35.270
And then they might save other gifts for home.
然后他们可能会把其他礼物留到家里再送。

1390
00:54:35.410 --> 00:54:38.150
But at Dunder Mifflin, they give each other something they made.
但在邓德·米夫林，他们会送给对方自己亲手做的东西。

1391
00:54:38.350 --> 00:54:38.670
Yes.
没错。

1392
00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:43.450
But, of course, this year, Pam has really gone all out there.
当然，今年帕姆确实是全力以赴了。

1393
00:54:43.630 --> 00:54:45.390
And she's made this comic book.
她做了这本漫画书。

1394
00:54:45.390 --> 00:54:47.990
And she's expecting that Jim has given her something.
她也期待着吉姆能送她点什么。

1395
00:54:48.030 --> 00:54:49.270
He gives her a box.
他给了她一个盒子。

1396
00:54:49.390 --> 00:54:50.670
And she shakes it.
她摇了摇。

1397
00:54:50.710 --> 00:54:53.370
And she says, oh, is it Pebbles from the Beach in Jamaica?
她说，噢，是牙买加海滩上的鹅卵石吗？

1398
00:54:53.590 --> 00:54:55.310
I loved how hard you shook the box.
我很喜欢你摇盒子的那股劲儿。

1399
00:54:55.310 --> 00:54:56.850
And he's like, hey, hey, hey, hey, hey.
而他就像是，嘿，嘿，嘿，嘿，嘿。

1400
00:54:57.650 --> 00:54:59.270
Well, she opens it.
好吧，她打开了盒子。

1401
00:54:59.390 --> 00:55:02.370
And it is a beautiful diamond tennis bracelet.
里面是一条漂亮的钻石网球手链。

1402
00:55:02.690 --> 00:55:05.230
That Pam is clearly not expecting.
帕姆显然没料到这一点。

1403
00:55:05.530 --> 00:55:05.990
No.
没错。

1404
00:55:06.230 --> 00:55:07.750
But Jim did have a good year.
但吉姆确实度过了不错的一年。

1405
00:55:07.950 --> 00:55:08.410
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1406
00:55:09.370 --> 00:55:12.790
We had a fan question from Michelle Q in Chicago.
我们收到了一位来自芝加哥的粉丝米歇尔·Q的提问。

1407
00:55:13.190 --> 00:55:16.950
Is the bracelet Jim gives Pam the same one she's wearing in the finale?
吉姆送给帕姆的那条手链，是她在结局里戴的那条吗？

1408
00:55:17.950 --> 00:55:19.110
Yes, it is.
是的，就是那条。

1409
00:55:19.350 --> 00:55:20.590
We saved this.
我们把它保存了下来。

1410
00:55:20.890 --> 00:55:26.510
Like we told you how every character had a wardrobe, had a closet in the wardrobe trailer.
就像我们之前说的，每个角色在服装拖车里都有一个专属衣柜。

1411
00:55:26.850 --> 00:55:28.830
Pam also had a jewelry box.
帕姆还有一个首饰盒。

1412
00:55:29.290 --> 00:55:35.430
And all of her most special things, her wedding rings and her watch and this bracelet, would
她所有最珍贵的东西，比如婚戒、手表还有这条手链，都会

1413
00:55:35.430 --> 00:55:35.930
live there.
放在那里。

1414
00:55:36.050 --> 00:55:39.910
And anytime there was an occasion to dress up, she would wear this bracelet.
每当有需要盛装打扮的场合，她就会戴上这条手链。

1415
00:55:40.330 --> 00:55:42.530
I love that Pam had a jewelry box.
我真喜欢帕姆有个首饰盒这件事。

1416
00:55:42.830 --> 00:55:44.850
Angela also had a jewelry box.
安吉拉也有一个首饰盒。

1417
00:55:45.410 --> 00:55:46.150
Oh, yeah?
哦，是吗？

1418
00:55:46.330 --> 00:55:46.510
Yeah.
是的。

1419
00:55:46.810 --> 00:55:48.490
It mostly was cat earrings.
里面大多是猫咪耳环。

1420
00:55:48.810 --> 00:55:50.430
And things like of that nature.
以及诸如此类的东西。

1421
00:55:50.630 --> 00:55:52.410
Things you might find at a cat con.
你在猫展上可能会看到的那种东西。

1422
00:55:52.730 --> 00:55:53.250
Exactly.
没错。

1423
00:55:53.250 --> 00:55:56.210
Pam is overwhelmed by this bracelet.
帕姆被这条手链感动得不知所措。

1424
00:55:56.370 --> 00:55:57.170
Moved to tears.
感动得热泪盈眶。

1425
00:55:57.410 --> 00:56:01.950
And now she is especially nervous about giving Jim her gift.
现在她对于送给吉姆礼物这件事感到格外紧张。

1426
00:56:02.610 --> 00:56:05.510
But, I mean, Jim loves it.
但是，我是说，吉姆很喜欢。

1427
00:56:05.670 --> 00:56:06.470
He loves it.
他非常喜欢。

1428
00:56:06.830 --> 00:56:06.890
He's speechless.
他感动得说不出话来。

1429
00:56:07.290 --> 00:56:07.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1430
00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:08.470
He loves her.
他爱她。

1431
00:56:08.770 --> 00:56:10.910
I want to backtrack for one second.
我想回过头来再说一点。

1432
00:56:11.170 --> 00:56:13.170
There was a scene I thought was so sweet.
有个场景我觉得特别温馨。

1433
00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:17.530
Michael is giving Woody a bath in the bathroom sink.
迈克尔在洗手池里给伍迪洗澡。

1434
00:56:17.530 --> 00:56:22.050
I think that sounds, hey now, hey now, Jenna.
我觉得听起来，嘿，等等，嘿，等等，珍娜。

1435
00:56:22.690 --> 00:56:23.710
The doll.
是那个玩偶。

1436
00:56:23.930 --> 00:56:25.370
He's giving the doll a bath.
他在给那个玩偶洗澡。

1437
00:56:25.710 --> 00:56:31.910
At 10 minutes, 51 seconds, there's a little tiny clothesline that Michael has made.
在10分51秒的时候，迈克尔做了一个小小的晾衣绳。

1438
00:56:32.050 --> 00:56:35.370
And Woody's clothes are hanging on it and his hat.
伍迪的衣服和帽子都挂在上面。

1439
00:56:35.370 --> 00:56:36.890
And it's the cutest thing.
那真是太可爱了。

1440
00:56:37.090 --> 00:56:42.030
I really loved Steve's performance in this little moment, I have to say.
我不得不说，我真的很喜欢史蒂夫在这个小片段里的表演。

1441
00:56:42.630 --> 00:56:47.070
He just was doing it so earnestly and honestly, there wasn't a lot behind it.
他演得那么真诚、那么质朴，没有太多复杂的潜台词。

1442
00:56:47.230 --> 00:56:48.810
He was cleaning it.
他就是在清洗它。

1443
00:56:48.970 --> 00:56:50.730
He was just trying to make something right.
他只是想把事情做好。

1444
00:56:50.970 --> 00:56:51.610
It was great.
太棒了。

1445
00:56:51.830 --> 00:56:55.630
And then he's going to try to sneak out of the office without saying goodbye.
然后他打算在不告别的情况下溜出办公室。

1446
00:56:55.910 --> 00:56:56.350
Yeah.
是的。

1447
00:56:56.590 --> 00:56:57.510
But Pam notices.
但帕姆注意到了。

1448
00:56:57.510 --> 00:56:58.990
She comes out after him.
她追了出来。

1449
00:56:59.530 --> 00:57:05.510
And she says, I shouldn't tell you this, but AJ won't commit to Holly.
她对他说，我不该告诉你这些，但AJ不愿给霍莉承诺。

1450
00:57:06.290 --> 00:57:08.190
And she's going to give him an ultimatum.
她打算给他下最后通牒。

1451
00:57:08.970 --> 00:57:14.070
She sort of says, I don't know a lot of happy marriages that start off with an ultimatum.
她大概是说，我没见过多少美满的婚姻是以最后通牒开始的。

1452
00:57:14.410 --> 00:57:16.470
And she tells Michael to just be patient.
她告诉迈克尔要耐心一点。

1453
00:57:16.470 --> 00:57:19.230
And he's like, yeah, I can do that.
他说，好的，我可以做到。

1454
00:57:20.270 --> 00:57:20.750
Yeah.
没错。

1455
00:57:20.910 --> 00:57:22.270
And they're going to walk back into gifts.
他们正要走回礼物区。

1456
00:57:29.580 --> 00:57:30.460
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1457
00:57:30.780 --> 00:57:31.260
Cassie.
凯西。

1458
00:57:31.920 --> 00:57:33.180
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1459
00:57:33.640 --> 00:57:34.720
She did it.
她做到了。

1460
00:57:37.210 --> 00:57:38.830
It took two weeks.
花了两个星期。

1461
00:57:39.010 --> 00:57:40.030
Cassie, get over here.
凯西，快过来。

1462
00:57:40.590 --> 00:57:41.830
Here it is, everybody.
大家看，在这儿。

1463
00:57:42.290 --> 00:57:43.510
The clacky balls are free.
这串碰撞球解开了。

1464
00:57:43.630 --> 00:57:43.810
Listen.
听着。

1465
00:57:45.330 --> 00:57:46.530
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1466
00:57:48.130 --> 00:57:52.030
Cassie, in two weeks, undid what a toddler did in 30 seconds.
凯西用了两周时间，解开了幼儿30秒就能弄乱的东西。

1467
00:57:52.470 --> 00:57:56.170
But I've had this a year and no one who came to my house could undo it.
但我这东西放了一年了，来我家的人没一个能解开。

1468
00:57:56.630 --> 00:57:57.070
Yay.
耶。

1469
00:57:57.830 --> 00:57:59.310
I can't believe that.
真不敢相信。

1470
00:57:59.510 --> 00:58:00.850
My kids are going to flip out.
我的孩子们一定会乐疯的。

1471
00:58:01.230 --> 00:58:02.290
Cade is going to flip out.
凯德一定会乐疯的。

1472
00:58:02.430 --> 00:58:03.990
Cade has worked the hardest at it.
凯德为了解开它最努力了。

1473
00:58:04.110 --> 00:58:05.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1474
00:58:05.210 --> 00:58:06.550
I didn't think it was going to happen.
我本来以为这事儿不会发生了。

1475
00:58:06.730 --> 00:58:09.370
And then it just, yeah, after a cocktail, it magically.
结果喝了杯鸡尾酒后，它就奇迹般地……

1476
00:58:10.730 --> 00:58:13.730
After the F train to Brooklyn, it magically happened.
坐完去布鲁克林的F线地铁后，奇迹就发生了。

1477
00:58:13.930 --> 00:58:15.190
It's a magic elixir.
这简直是魔法药水。

1478
00:58:15.750 --> 00:58:17.570
I mean, my kids are going to freak out.
我是说，我的孩子们一定会大吃一惊的。

1479
00:58:17.730 --> 00:58:19.670
Like, they have tried so hard.
他们真的尝试了很久。

1480
00:58:19.770 --> 00:58:21.070
One visit from Santa cans.
圣诞老人来访一次就搞定了。

1481
00:58:21.330 --> 00:58:21.950
I know.
我知道。

1482
00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:22.730
Wow.
哇。

1483
00:58:23.290 --> 00:58:24.410
What an episode.
真是精彩的一集。

1484
00:58:24.750 --> 00:58:25.070
Woo.
喔。

1485
00:58:25.590 --> 00:58:27.210
That scared the crap out of me.
刚才吓死我了。

1486
00:58:27.210 --> 00:58:29.550
I know because Angela's back is to the door.
我知道，因为安吉拉背对着门。

1487
00:58:29.710 --> 00:58:31.050
So I didn't see Cassie.
所以我没看见凯西。

1488
00:58:31.190 --> 00:58:31.910
You were just screaming.
你刚才一直在尖叫。

1489
00:58:31.910 --> 00:58:35.030
Yeah, there was a Michael Myers element to it where she was behind you all of a sudden.
没错，刚才那一下真有迈克尔·迈尔斯的感觉，她突然就出现在你身后了。

1490
00:58:35.130 --> 00:58:37.190
Is someone going to attack me?
会有人袭击我吗？

1491
00:58:37.490 --> 00:58:37.890
Okay.
好吧。

1492
00:58:38.770 --> 00:58:40.110
I don't know where we were.
我不记得我们刚才说到哪儿了。

1493
00:58:40.610 --> 00:58:44.490
Well, I believe Michael was about to give Kelly her gift.
嗯，我想迈克尔正准备把礼物给凯利。

1494
00:58:44.490 --> 00:58:48.010
Yes, Michael and Pam have come back into the party.
没错，迈克尔和帕姆回到了派对上。

1495
00:58:48.330 --> 00:58:53.150
At 15 minutes, 12 seconds, we have a really hardcore fakie bag.
在15分12秒的时候，我们看到了一个非常明显的假纸袋。

1496
00:58:53.610 --> 00:58:54.150
Oh.
噢。

1497
00:58:54.570 --> 00:58:55.350
It's a fakie paper bag.
那是个假纸袋。

1498
00:58:55.350 --> 00:58:56.530
I can't believe I missed it.
真不敢相信我竟然错过了。

1499
00:58:56.650 --> 00:58:57.950
Oh, it's substantial.
噢，它看起来很厚实。

1500
00:58:58.310 --> 00:59:05.150
But as Michael is trying to re-gift this Hello Kitty laptop sleeve, he overhears Holly and AJ.
但当迈克尔试图把这个Hello Kitty笔记本电脑包转送出去时，他无意中听到了霍莉和AJ的对话。

1501
00:59:05.610 --> 00:59:09.070
Yeah, AJ finds the Woody towel and he says, it smells.
没错，AJ发现了那个胡迪毛巾，他说，这东西有味道。

1502
00:59:09.090 --> 00:59:09.990
What happened?
发生了什么？

1503
00:59:10.310 --> 00:59:13.910
And Holly makes up a total lie to protect Michael.
霍莉为了保护迈克尔编了一个弥天大谎。

1504
00:59:14.170 --> 00:59:17.970
She said it was her that spilled salad dressing on Woody.
她说伍迪身上的沙拉酱是她洒的。

1505
00:59:18.210 --> 00:59:19.610
Blue cheese salad dressing.
蓝纹奶酪沙拉酱。

1506
00:59:19.750 --> 00:59:20.630
Yeah, stinko.
没错，臭烘烘的。

1507
00:59:21.010 --> 00:59:22.310
Michael kind of smiles.
迈克尔露出了那种笑容。

1508
00:59:22.310 --> 00:59:26.350
He realizes, you know, she's protecting him.
他意识到，你知道的，她在保护他。

1509
00:59:27.270 --> 00:59:29.150
Michael is going to come through for Jada.
迈克尔打算帮贾达实现愿望。

1510
00:59:29.390 --> 00:59:33.470
He dresses up as the original Santa from the first part of the Christmas party.
他打扮成圣诞派对前半段里那个最初的圣诞老人。

1511
00:59:33.710 --> 00:59:35.870
And he asks her, what do you want for Christmas?
他问她，你圣诞节想要什么？

1512
00:59:36.050 --> 00:59:37.230
It's a very sweet moment.
那是一个非常温馨的时刻。

1513
00:59:37.770 --> 00:59:38.850
Holly clocks it.
霍莉注意到了这一点。

1514
00:59:39.130 --> 00:59:40.530
It makes us all hopeful.
这让我们都感到充满希望。

1515
00:59:41.070 --> 00:59:41.530
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1516
00:59:42.130 --> 00:59:45.970
And the episode is going to end with such a creepy scene.
而这一集的结尾将是一个非常诡异的场景。

1517
00:59:46.810 --> 00:59:48.990
Yeah, Jim doesn't want to leave the office.
是啊，吉姆不想离开办公室。

1518
00:59:49.230 --> 00:59:51.230
Earlier, he tried to form a truce with Dwight.
早些时候，他试图和德怀特休战。

1519
00:59:51.230 --> 00:59:52.590
Dwight did not accept.
德怀特没有接受。

1520
00:59:53.270 --> 00:59:55.290
And he has to leave now.
现在他必须得走了。

1521
00:59:55.450 --> 00:59:55.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1522
00:59:55.730 --> 00:59:56.590
And he's scared.
而且他很害怕。

1523
00:59:56.850 --> 01:00:03.510
Remember the last time he was down in the parking lot, Dwight hid in a snowman and pelted him with snowballs until his nose was bleeding?
还记得上次他在停车场时，德怀特躲在雪人里，用雪球砸得他鼻血直流吗？

1524
01:00:03.850 --> 01:00:04.050
Yeah.
记得。

1525
01:00:04.410 --> 01:00:04.650
Right.
没错。

1526
01:00:05.010 --> 01:00:07.150
Pam is like, come on, it'll be fine.
帕姆说，来吧，会没事的。

1527
01:00:07.170 --> 01:00:08.490
And then they step outside.
然后他们走了出去。

1528
01:00:18.810 --> 01:00:19.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1529
01:00:19.770 --> 01:00:20.310
Yeah, you're right.
是啊，你说得对。

1530
01:00:20.390 --> 01:00:24.750
It's like some weird part of Squid Game where, you know, they're going to attack you.
就像《鱿鱼游戏》里那种奇怪的环节，你知道的，他们会攻击你。

1531
01:00:25.070 --> 01:00:27.030
We had a fan question from Kaylee D.
我们收到了一位来自加拿大蒙特利尔的粉丝凯莉·D的提问，她问，停车场场景里的雪人是用什么做的？

1532
01:00:27.150 --> 01:00:31.350
in Montreal, Canada, who said, what were the snowmen made of in the parking lot scene?
在洛杉矶的气温下你们是怎么做到的？

1533
01:00:31.690 --> 01:00:33.309
How do you do this in the L.A.
凯莉，我们上周讨论了很多关于这个的问题，因为我们拍摄这一集的那周天气非常热。

1534
01:00:33.309 --> 01:00:34.010
temperatures?
这些雪人是用真正的雪做的。

1535
01:00:34.670 --> 01:00:40.790
Kaylee, we talked a lot about this last week because it was very warm the week we were filming this episode.
执导这一集的雷恩·威尔逊说，这一集的雪景特效需要100吨碎冰。

1536
01:00:40.790 --> 01:00:43.430
And these snowmen were made out of real snow.
哇。

1537
01:00:44.450 --> 01:00:52.070
Rainn Wilson, who directed this episode, said that the snow effects for this episode required 100 tons of chipped ice.
为了制作这些雪人，特效团队制作了金属模具，然后手工填实。

1538
01:00:52.870 --> 01:00:53.210
Wow.
但与上一集中背部开口以便德怀特钻进去的雪人不同，你会发现这些是完整的雪人。

1539
01:00:53.210 --> 01:01:01.150
In order to make these snowmen, the special effects team had built the metal molds and they hand-packed them.
没错，因为他们要穿过这些雪人。

1540
01:01:01.370 --> 01:01:09.530
But unlike the one in the previous episode where the back was open so that Dwight could get in, you notice these are full snowmen.
嗯哼。

1541
01:01:09.710 --> 01:01:10.810
Right, because they run through them.
吉姆用雨伞攻击它们，它们非常结实。

1542
01:01:10.890 --> 01:01:11.310
Mm-hmm.
明迪说这些雪人花了一整天时间才建好。

1543
01:01:11.550 --> 01:01:15.050
And Jim, like, is attacking them with the umbrella and they're dense.
而且还需要大量的维护。

1544
01:01:15.590 --> 01:01:18.450
Mindy said the snowmen took an entire day to build.
他们最担心的事情就是脚印。

1545
01:01:18.990 --> 01:01:20.870
And they also took a lot of maintenance.
他们必须确保脚印看起来只有一个人留下的。

1546
01:01:21.030 --> 01:01:24.070
And the biggest thing that they had to worry about were footprints.
所以，你知道，尽管需要很多人来放置这些雪人，但看起来必须像是德怀特自己做的。

1547
01:01:24.930 --> 01:01:28.490
They had to make sure that the footprints were only one person.
天哪。

1548
01:01:28.790 --> 01:01:35.230
So, you know, even though it took many people to place all these snowmen, it had to look like Dwight did it himself.
这就是对细节的关注，各位。

1549
01:01:35.590 --> 01:01:36.770
Oh, my gosh.
兰迪·科德雷说，对于整集节目，人工、材料、真雪和假雪，制作所有的雪人，

1550
01:01:36.890 --> 01:01:38.750
That's attention to detail, folks.
这真是太细致了。

1551
01:01:39.290 --> 01:01:45.510
Randy Cordray said for this whole episode, labor, materials, real and fake snow, making all the snowmen,
这就是对细节的把控，朋友们。

1552
01:01:45.510 --> 01:01:48.890
the special effects budget was over $65,000.
特效预算超过了65,000美元。

1553
01:01:49.610 --> 01:01:50.950
Well, there was a lot.
嗯，确实有很多。

1554
01:01:51.410 --> 01:01:52.490
There was a lot.
确实有很多。

1555
01:01:52.750 --> 01:01:53.690
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1556
01:01:54.090 --> 01:01:54.350
What?
怎么着？

1557
01:01:54.650 --> 01:01:56.530
No one's going to pop out of these snowmen.
没人会从这些雪人里跳出来。

1558
01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:58.870
Dwight is actually up on the roof.
德怀特其实在屋顶上。

1559
01:01:59.630 --> 01:02:03.010
And he says, in the end, the greatest snowball is fear.
他说，归根结底，最棒的雪球就是恐惧。

1560
01:02:03.250 --> 01:02:04.250
Merry Christmas.
圣诞快乐。

1561
01:02:05.610 --> 01:02:07.830
And that's how the episode ends.
这一集就是这样结束的。

1562
01:02:08.010 --> 01:02:08.250
Yeah.
是啊。

1563
01:02:08.810 --> 01:02:11.510
Pam and Jim are, like, just trying to make their way to their car.
帕姆和吉姆当时就像是在努力走向他们的车。

1564
01:02:11.670 --> 01:02:13.310
Jim starts attacking the snowmen.
吉姆开始攻击那些雪人。

1565
01:02:13.310 --> 01:02:16.130
And we had a final fan question from Grace B.
我们还收到了来自阿肯色州克林顿市的格蕾丝·B发来的最后一个粉丝提问。

1566
01:02:16.210 --> 01:02:16.990
in Clinton, Arkansas.
在阿肯色州的克林顿。

1567
01:02:17.650 --> 01:02:19.870
How did Jim and Pam get out of the parking lot?
吉姆和帕姆是怎么离开停车场的？

1568
01:02:19.930 --> 01:02:21.030
That was my question!
那也是我的问题！

1569
01:02:21.270 --> 01:02:22.810
Because it's solid snowmen.
因为那是实心的雪人。

1570
01:02:22.930 --> 01:02:24.510
They would have had to driven through it.
他们本得开车撞过去才行。

1571
01:02:25.010 --> 01:02:25.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1572
01:02:25.850 --> 01:02:27.590
Grace said, this keeps me up at night.
格蕾丝说，这个问题让她彻夜难眠。

1573
01:02:27.850 --> 01:02:28.930
Yeah, me too, Grace.
是啊，我也是，格蕾丝。

1574
01:02:29.230 --> 01:02:32.670
Grace, once I read your question and watched the scene, now it's all I can think of.
格蕾丝，我读了你的问题并重看了那一幕后，现在满脑子都是这个问题。

1575
01:02:32.690 --> 01:02:33.610
I can't unsee it.
我无法不去想它。

1576
01:02:33.730 --> 01:02:34.490
Yeah, me too.
是啊，我也是。

1577
01:02:34.970 --> 01:02:37.390
Well, that was classy Christmas, too, everyone.
好吧，那也是“优雅的圣诞节”，各位。

1578
01:02:37.650 --> 01:02:39.610
Next week, we're going to be back with Ultimatum.
下周我们将回归，讨论“最后通牒”那一集。

1579
01:02:39.670 --> 01:02:40.490
It is so good.
那一集非常棒。

1580
01:02:40.490 --> 01:02:47.190
A big thank you to Josh Snyder for this amazing F Train to Brooklyn drink.
非常感谢乔什·斯奈德为我们调制了这款超棒的“F线去布鲁克林”饮品。

1581
01:02:47.550 --> 01:02:52.490
Thank you, Angela and Cade, for going to the CatCon and bringing us these lovely gifts.
谢谢安吉拉和凯德去参加猫咪大会并带回这些可爱的礼物。

1582
01:02:52.610 --> 01:02:54.290
And Martha Stewart, thank you!
还有玛莎·斯图尔特，谢谢你！

1583
01:02:55.230 --> 01:03:00.230
Thank you so much for designing a short-sleeve puffer jacket that you call a puffer tee.
非常感谢你设计了一款短袖羽绒外套，你称之为羽绒T恤。

1584
01:03:00.670 --> 01:03:03.210
Yes, because it looks like a t-shirt, but it's a puffer.
没错，因为它看起来像T恤，但它是羽绒材质的。

1585
01:03:03.330 --> 01:03:06.010
But t-shirts don't have zippers down the front of them.
但T恤前面没有拉链。

1586
01:03:06.010 --> 01:03:06.750
This one does, Jenna.
这件有，珍娜。

1587
01:03:07.270 --> 01:03:07.790
How dare you?
你怎么敢？

1588
01:03:07.790 --> 01:03:09.110
Which is why it's not a t-shirt.
所以它才不是T恤。

1589
01:03:09.110 --> 01:03:11.390
We also would like to thank Randy Cordray.
我们还要感谢兰迪·科德雷。

1590
01:03:11.610 --> 01:03:14.830
Every week, he gives us the best behind-the-scenes details.
他每周都为我们提供最棒的幕后细节。

1591
01:03:15.030 --> 01:03:15.910
We love you, Randy.
我们爱你，兰迪。

1592
01:03:16.210 --> 01:03:20.570
And of course, Tone Rodriguez, thank you so much for telling us about your comic book.
当然还有托恩·罗德里格斯，非常感谢你告诉我们关于你漫画书的事。

1593
01:03:20.770 --> 01:03:24.650
And to Cassie for undoing the clacky balls.
还要感谢卡西帮我们解开了那些咔哒响的球。

1594
01:03:25.030 --> 01:03:26.110
This was a big week.
这一周过得很充实。

1595
01:03:26.330 --> 01:03:27.310
It was a big episode.
这一集内容很丰富。

1596
01:03:27.530 --> 01:03:28.530
You guys have a great week.
祝大家度过愉快的一周。

1597
01:03:28.630 --> 01:03:29.590
We'll see you next time.
我们下次见。

1598
01:03:29.710 --> 01:03:30.090
See you then.
到时候见。

1599
01:03:30.090 --> 01:03:37.080
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

